# Issue tracker: GitLab

Issues and MRDs for `{{ project }}` live as GitLab issues. Use the `glab` CLI.

## Conventions

- **Create**: `glab issue create --title "..." --description "..."`.
- **Read**: `glab issue view <number> --comments`.
- **List**: `glab issue list --label "~needs-triage"`.
- **Label**: `glab issue update <number> --label "..."` / `--unlabel "..."`.
- **Close**: `glab issue close <number>`, or write `Closes #NN` on its own line
  at the bottom of a merge request so the merge closes it automatically.

Infer the project from `git remote -v`; `glab` resolves it inside a clone.

When a skill says "publish to the issue tracker", create a GitLab issue.
When it says "fetch the relevant ticket", run `glab issue view <number> --comments`.
